  "bio": "Abdan is the pet name by which Abdullah ibn Uthman of Marw is always known; a reader who does not recognise it may fail to match him with his full name. A wealthy client of the Azd who gave a million dirhams in charity, he was Ibn al-Mubarak's closest transmitter and copied out his books himself. Al-Bukhari heard a great deal from him; of the six compilers only Ibn Majah has nothing through him.",
